# Yuztoo Website Holy Books

This branch (`site-web`) is the **public Yuztoo website only** (`yuztoo.com`). It never imports
Flutter app code or CRM code.

Stack: **Vite 6 + React 18, plain JavaScript (`.js` / `.jsx`, no TypeScript), no router**, every
page prerendered to static HTML and served by Firebase Hosting.

Before writing or reviewing code, follow the matching book in `docs/holy-books/` and run its PR
checklist:

- Folders, routes, content modules, data access → `docs/holy-books/DDD_HOLY_BOOK.md`
- Colors, typography, contrast, surfaces → `docs/holy-books/BRAND_HOLY_BOOK.md`
- Firestore rules, Cloud Functions, public/token pages, headers, HTML rendering → `docs/holy-books/SECURITY_HOLY_BOOK.md`
- Pages, meta, JSON-LD, sitemap, robots, redirects, forms → `docs/holy-books/SEO_HOLY_BOOK.md`
- Prerendering, bundles, images, Firebase reads, Core Web Vitals → `docs/holy-books/PERFORMANCE_HOLY_BOOK.md`
- Layout on every screen size, 320 → 1920 px (non-negotiable) → `docs/holy-books/RESPONSIVE_HOLY_BOOK.md`

Hard rules that apply to every change:

- Nothing outside `src/data/**` (and `src/lib/**`) may import from `lib/firebase` or call our
  backend with raw `fetch`.
- Every indexable page ships prerendered HTML — never an empty `<div id="root">` — and is listed
  in `src/routes.js`.
- Security is enforced server-side (Firestore rules, Cloud Functions, Hosting headers). Hiding a
  control in the UI is not security.
- Page copy, image `src` and `alt` live in `<page>Content.js`, never inline in a component.
- Colors come from `var(--token)` in `src/global.css`, copied from the Flutter app. No raw hex in
  a component, and gold is an accent — never a large fill or body text on light.
- The market is **France (Belfort)**, the audiences are **commerçants, clients, collectivités**,
  and the locale is `fr-FR`. Never `fr_MA`.
- Each book has a **Known gaps** section. When you close a gap, delete it in the same PR; when
  you find one, add it.
